<title>DUBAI: Saudi British Bank Q1 net profit rises.</title>
<headline>Saudi British Bank Q1 net profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			  (million riyals unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		  123.28	 vs     106.99</p>
<p>    Net operating income    118.88	 vs     112.32</p>
<p>    Investment income	 221.87	 vs     133.74</p>
<p>    Provisions		   18.51	 vs	12.99</p>
<p>Full name: The Saudi British Bank.</p>
<p>Note - The figures are unaudited.</p>
<p>The Riyadh-based bank is 40 percent owned by HSBC Holdings Plc. The rest is held by Saudi Arabian investors.</p>
<p>The bank said liquidity continued to grow strongly over the first quarter thanks to the continuing settlements of arrears payments by the government to the private sector, along with an overall improvement in business confidence in Saudi Arabia.</p>
<p>It expected the trend to continue resulting in an eventual improvement in demand for loans and advances in the second half.</p>
<p>-- Dubai newsroom +9714-626990</p>
</text>
